                <pb facs="0682" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg594"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Barrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis instructs Mr. Barrett to assure the Government of Panama that the
                    United States Government will do nothing inconsistent with the honor and true
                    interests of both Republics; that it will assist and uphold Panama in every
                    proper way, and that it will not adopt at this time any permanent policy without
                    fully consulting Panama.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
